            "n_events": 21,
            "result_text": "I'll help you set up a git server with automatic deployment to a web server. Here's a complete setup:\n\n## Server-side Configuration\n\n**1. Create a bare git repository**\n```bash\nmkdir -p /git/server\ncd /git/server\ngit init --bare\n```\n\n**2. Create a post-receive hook for automatic deployment**\n\nCreate `/git/server/hooks/post-receive`:\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\nDEPLOY_DIR=\"/var/www/html\"\nmkdir -p $DEPLOY_DIR\ncd $DEPLOY_DIR\ngit clone --bare /git/server .git\ngit config --bool core.bare false\ngit reset --hard HEAD\n```\n\nMake it executable:\n```bash\nchmod +x /git/server/hooks/post-receive\n```\n\n**3. Set up the web server**\n\nStart a simple Python HTTP server on port 8080:\n```bash\nmkdir -p /var/www/html\ncd /var/www/html\npython3 -m http.server 8080\n```\n\nOr use nginx (more production-ready). Create `/etc/nginx/sites-available/default`:\n```nginx\nserver {\n    listen 8080 default_server;\n    server_name _;\n    root /var/www/html;\n    index index.html;\n    location / {\n        try_files $uri $uri/ =404;\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThen start nginx:\n```bash\nsudo systemctl start nginx\n```\n\n## Client-side Workflow\n\nOnce set up, your workflow becomes:\n```bash\ngit clone user@server:/git/server my-project\ncd my-project\necho \"hello world\" > hello.html\ngit add hello.html\ngit commit -m \"add hello.html\"\ngit push origin master\n```\n\nThen test:\n```bash\ncurl http://server:8080/hello.html\n```\n\n**Key points:**\n- The bare repository at `/git/server` acts as the central remote\n- The `post-receive` hook automatically checks out to `/var/www/html` whenever you push\n- The web server serves files from `/var/www/html`\n- This is a simple \"push-to-deploy\" system\n\nWould you like me to adjust this for a different web server setup, or do you need help with any specific part?"
